screen: baseline
theme: Dark
headline: Passive baseline
caption: Equal-weight buy-and-hold across 10 large-cap pairs, bought once at year-open and never rebalanced. Gross of costs — no fees, no slippage, no funding — so a tradeable buy-and-hold would have kept less. Passive baseline; active ≤ passive in the reachable universe, this sample.
year_chips:
  [2023] active color=accent(dark) bg=panel_raised
  [2024] inactive color=fg_muted
kpi_strip:
  total_return: 196.22% color=pos
  cagr: 196.22%
  sharpe: 1.8417
  max_dd: −34.57% color=neg
  win_rate: —
  trades: 0
sharpe_note: Sharpe 1.84 is the realized single-path figure for 2023 — the one actual price sequence this curve draws. The published passive bar is the bootstrap median (p50) 1.74 over 200 block-resampled paths.
curve+band:
  state: ready points=366
  peak: 326978.55 trough: 100000.00 max_dd_frac: 0.333060584869292017194007451
  band_axis_max_pct: 33.31
  curve_line=ACCENT curve_fill=UP_500
  band_line=DOWN_500 band_fill=DOWN_500
sampling_note: Cards are hourly-resolution metrics; the curve and band are drawn from the daily-sampled CSV (366 rows), which misses intraday extremes — its deepest visible drawdown is 33.31% against the card's 34.57%.
risk_detail: Sortino 2.51 / Calmar 5.68 (2023)
